<title>UK: British civil servant numbers continue to fall.</title>
<headline>British civil servant numbers continue to fall.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of British civil servants has fallen by 34 percent to 486,800 since the Conservatives took power in 1979, official figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the latest quarter to end-September, the total fell one percent following the switch of several executive agencies to the private sector, the Office of Public Service said.</p>
